# Tracecheck

Tracecheck is a privacy-first website scanner. It checks public HTML and response headers for tracker signals, fingerprinting APIs, cookies, third-party resources, detected technologies, and security headers.

## New in this version

- Browser-assisted scan with Playwright fallback
- Report persistence via local JSON store in development
- Report history endpoint
- Report lookup by ID
- Optional OpenAI-backed chat assistant grounded in the latest scan
- Discord webhook notification for scan events
- Graceful fallback when AI is not configured

## Environment variables

Add these in Vercel under Project Settings → Environment Variables:

```text
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/...
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
```

## Local run

```bash
npm install
npx playwright install chromium
npx vercel dev
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

## Endpoints

```text
POST /api/scan
GET /api/history?limit=10
GET /api/report?id=<report-id>
POST /api/chat
```

## Safety

This tool does not execute JavaScript in the default path unless Playwright is successfully available in the environment. It blocks credentials, localhost, private/reserved IPs, non-HTTP protocols, and oversized responses. It is intended as evidence-based analysis, not proof of how a website stores or uses data.
